PROCESS SERVER INFORMATION

Anyone interested in becoming a certified process server in the Third Judicial Circuit should carefully review this information page, Administrative Order No. 2026-006, and the application packet.

The current contact information for Court Administration in the Third Judicial Circuit:

Columbia County Courthouse
173 NE Hernando Avenue, RM 408
Lake City, Florida 32055
Phone: (386) 754-7107

Designated Employee: Lisa Butler, Human Resources Analyst II

Fees and Method of Payment:
The initial certification fee is $100.00. The renewal certification fee is $75.00.    These fees are nonrefundable and are due each year upon initial certification or renewal.
The certification fee must be paid by cashier’s check or money order and made out to “State of Florida”.
The applicant will need to provide an annual criminal history background investigation through FDLE at the applicant’s expense. The following is the FDLE website: http://www.fdle.state.fl.us/. (Request criminal history) The certified results must be mailed to Lisa Butler at the mailing address above.
New civil process server applicants are required to complete a class and exam through The Florida Association of Professional Process Servers (FAPPS.) The website is as follows: https://www.fapps.org/afpscourseschedule.aspx Here you will find the dates and times that classes are available. For new applicants, the 16-hour course will be mandatory, and for annual renewals, the 4-hour continuing education course will be mandatory. Both are available to be taken by Zoom.
A completed application packet should include (1) the four-page application, (2) the Statement of Policy Regarding Conduct of Certified Process Servers, (3) the Certified Process Server Agreement, (4) the Certificate of Good Conduct, and (5) the certification fee.
For new certifications, the applicant can mail, or hand deliver to the address listed above, the following application materials: application, certification fee and passport photos. (Certified results from the FDLE criminal background history must be mailed to Lisa Butler at the mailing address above)
Once a new applicant has completed their FAPPS class, the certificate needs to be forwarded to this office along with a Bond naming “Administrative Office of the Courts, Third Judicial Circuit” as the Obligee in the amount of $5,000.00. When all required documents have been submitted, the certified civil process server will be sworn in, and a badge and an order signed by the Chief Judge will be issued.
For annual renewals, each civil process server must submit the renewal fee, updated bond, updated passport photo, yearly FDLE background investigation report and proof of the required 4-hour continuing education course from FAPPS.
If you have any questions about the Certified Process Server Program, please direct those questions to Lisa Butler, at the address or phone number listed above.
